SR-RX recipe patch 0004 (+lab): no -march=native in the root CMakeLists.txt.
Pinned SatDump 1aedd60 adds -march=native to CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS whenever the CI environment variable
is not defined (CMakeLists.txt:166-172, with the warning "Will likely not be portable to other systems"),
and its first set() also replaces CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS with CMAKE_C_FLAGS, which drops -fopenmp. The lab
builder runs CMake with a clean environment (build_recipe.py), so the package would target the arm64
CI runner, not the QCS6490. With this change the flags are those of upstream CI builds.
SatDump is GPL-3.0 (upstream LICENSE, git blob f288702d2fa16d3cdf0035b15a9fcbc552cd88e7). This change is distributed under the same licence.
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -163,7 +163,9 @@
     link_directories(windows/deps/output/bin)
 endif()
 
-if((NOT DEFINED ENV{CI}) AND NOT DEFINED ANDROID)
+# SR-RX +lab: never -march=native. The lab builder runs CMake with a clean environment (no CI), so this
+# block would target the build machine's CPU instead of the Q6A and replace CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS (-fopenmp).
+if(FALSE)
     if(APPLE OR UNIX)
         message("-- Not running on CI. Building for native architecture! Will likely not be portable to other systems.")
         set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} -march=native")    
